# CI before push

As a general rule, do not treat backend or frontend work as done until the same checks as `.github/workflows/ci.yml` pass locally.

## When to run

- After substantive changes under `backend/` or `frontend/`.
- Before suggesting the user commit, push, or open a pull request.
- When the user asks to commit or push: run checks first unless they explicitly skip.

## Command (repo root)

```bash
./bin/ci-check.sh
```

Firestore emulator integration (optional, needs Java): `./bin/ci-check.sh --integration`

## Parity with CI

| Job | Local command |
| --- | --- |
| Backend | `npm audit --omit=dev --audit-level=high`, then `lint`, `test`, `build`, `smoke` in `backend/` |
| Frontend | corepack npm 11.11.0, `npm audit --audit-level=high`, then `lint`, `test -- --watch=false`, `build`, `smoke` in `frontend/` |
| Integration | only with `--integration`; runs `backend` `test:emulators` |

Use Node 22+ (match CI).

## On failure

Fix the failure and re-run `./bin/ci-check.sh` until green. Do not tell the user to push with known CI failures.

## Git hooks

- `pre-commit`: frontend `lint-staged` only (fast).
- `pre-push`: runs `./bin/ci-check.sh`. Bypass hook only: `SKIP_CI=1 git push`.

Run `--integration` when changing Firestore rules, emulator tests, or backend integration code—not on every UI tweak.
